---
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  updated={site.legalUpdated}
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Which cookies and browser storage ToolKade uses for site settings, analytics and advertising, and how you can control or remove them in your browser."
>
  <p>
    This page explains how {site.name} uses cookies and similar technologies such as your browser's local
    storage.
  </p>

  <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files a website stores in your browser. Local storage is a similar feature that
    lets a site save small amounts of data on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>What we use</h2>
  <h3>Settings stored on your device</h3>
  <p>
    We use local storage to remember your preferences, such as dark mode and the last values you entered in a
    tool. This data never leaves your device and is not used for tracking.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics cookies</h3>
  <p>
    We may use analytics cookies to count visits and see which pages are popular, so we can improve the site.
    These are set only where you have agreed to them if the law requires consent.
  </p>

  <h3>Advertising cookies</h3>
  <p>
    We may show ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads based on
    your previous visits to this and other websites. You can manage personalised ads at
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Google Ads Settings
    </a>
    . Learn more in our
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies and clear local storage in your browser settings. If you block them, the
    tools will still work, but your preferences will not be remembered between visits.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
